{"ablation":{"active":false,"kind":"none","note":""},"arm_id":"amb1-case01-product-scope-primary","assistant_contributions":[{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-001","speaker":"assistant","text":"The immediate distinction is whether Northline is revealing a broader need or buying influence over a small team. I would not decide from the size of the account alone. Ask what exact job the workspace enables, what they do today, and which parts could serve other customers. In parallel, make the reliability and roadmap cost visible. If the request consumes the same people who own those commitments, “we can probably fit it in” is already a choice to delay them.","turn_number":1},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-002","speaker":"assistant","text":"Fair correction. Their request may be both a relationship obligation and a legitimate product lead. Lina's judgment and motivation are evidence, but not yet evidence that the remaining thirty percent—or the support expectations around it—will stay contained. A short technical and workflow discovery could separate the reusable layer from Northline-specific behavior. I would frame that as learning, not as a quiet commitment to build the whole workspace.","turn_number":2},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-003","speaker":"assistant","text":"Then discovery needs an explicit boundary before it starts: what question you are investigating, how long you will investigate it, and what decisions remain open afterward. You could tell Northline that the team is evaluating whether a reusable reporting foundation fits the product, not scheduling their requested workspace. That may disappoint them, but it is clearer than relying on different interpretations of “summer path.” Your sales lead should be part of that reset so the company speaks with one voice.","turn_number":3},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-004","speaker":"assistant","text":"You do not need to present a governance ceremony. The substance can be human: acknowledge what they have contributed, explain that you are genuinely interested, and be honest that the team has other promises and reliability debt. The boundary can live in your internal plan and in a plain sentence to them. Something like, “We want to understand this properly, but I do not want our curiosity to sound like a delivery promise.” That preserves gratitude without converting gratitude into unlimited scope.","turn_number":4},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-005","speaker":"assistant","text":"That makes this partly a sequencing and ownership question, not only feature selection. Lina's energy is a real resource, but it should not make the reliability burden disappear for other people. One possible design is to time-box her investigation while another owner defines the minimum reliability work that cannot slip, then reconvene with actual effort and ownership. But if the team cannot staff both without wishful allocation, the experiment will not solve the conflict; it will merely postpone naming it.","turn_number":5},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-006","speaker":"assistant","text":"The new email separates two clocks: delivery can wait, but access to a knowledgeable collaborator may not. That supports a narrower move—capture the workflow and test the reusable concept now without beginning full implementation. It also strengthens the case for protecting the smaller-customer and reliability commitments, since their demand is current and repeated. The open question is whether your team can conduct discovery without it becoming an unofficial project through momentum alone.","turn_number":6},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-007","speaker":"assistant","text":"That plan protects the learning opportunity without pretending the underlying tradeoff is resolved. The two risks you named remain real: restricting prototypes may make discovery artificial, while careful language may still feel like distance to Northline. You can decide in advance what kind of disposable prototype is allowed and ask Northline to reflect back what they believe the sessions mean. Neither step guarantees trust or a good product decision, but both make misunderstanding easier to notice before momentum chooses for you.","turn_number":7}],"boundary":{"all_assistant_messages_included":true,"assistant_mentions_are_not_deterministic_resolution":true,"assistant_semantic_prefilter":false,"assistant_source_evidence_text_included":true,"deterministic_semantic_merge":false,"expected_patterns_included":false,"fact_free_routing_projection_required":true,"graph_model_names_included":false,"graph_runtime_effect":"none","multiple_coherent_records_per_role_preserved":true,"raw_user_conversation_included":false,"user_role_semantic_prose_included":true},"case_id":"amb1-case01-product-scope","controlled_mechanisms":["acknowledged_constraint_not_gated","ambiguous_signal_treated_as_commitment","counterpressure_acknowledged_not_integrated","criteria_defined_after_commitment","initial_frame_persists_after_question_change","missing_reversal_condition","reversible_path_not_considered","status_signal_used_as_evidence","upside_downside_evidence_asymmetry"],"packet_sha256":"1a5d28c0adc10f5c93784b5d0c7184291992175cb6ce691ce5199c5ef4141713","qualification_review":{"evidence_ids":["e049","e061"],"interpretation":"The user remains explicitly unresolved on whether banning production-grade code during discovery will stifle Lina's learning process or if Northline will still interpret the cautious approach as a polite 'no'. They also note the looming risk of losing their primary champion if they wait too long.","limitations":"These concerns represent inherent path-dependencies and risks that the provisional plan fails to fully neutralize.","outcome":"unresolved_qualification_present"},"role_records":[{"evidence_ids":["e004","e005","e011","e012","e014","e015"],"fidelity_note":"The starting position showcases the product manager's internal tension: they appreciate the customer's loyalty and early support, and are inclined to trust the developer's motivation and the potential for a reusable reporting layer, but are highly constrained by postponed engineering tasks (reliability backlog) and outstanding promises to smaller customers.","limitations":"The initial turn shows the user's indecision; we can only view their starting position as a balance of conflicting values (customer relationship and developer excitement versus roadmap integrity and service reliability) rather than a planned action.","role":"starting","role_interpretation":"The user starts in a state of conflict and hesitation, vacillating between accommodating a crucial long-term customer's unique reporting request (which could yield a general reporting layer) and honoring existing commitments to smaller customers and reliability backlogs. The user actively defends the customer against being characterized as demanding and values their lead developer's excitement about the underlying technology.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-starting-01-af74f2929a0f94","semantic_status":"supported","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e005","stance_expression_kind":"uncertain_or_undecided","stance_object_interpretation":"Whether to adapt the roadmap for Northline's reporting workspace request or reject it as custom distraction.","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e004","stance_expression_kind":"counterpressure","stance_object_interpretation":"Postponing reliability work and core workflow improvements already promised to other customers.","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e012","stance_expression_kind":"held_assessment","stance_object_interpretation":"Northline has been patient through rough releases and is a highly supportive early collaborator rather than just a demanding voice.","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e015","stance_expression_kind":"held_assessment","stance_object_interpretation":"Lina's technical excitement and her view that most of the work can build a general reporting layer are critical considerations.","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"}]},{"evidence_ids":["e057","e058","e059","e060"],"fidelity_note":"Captures the user's specific provisional framework at the end of the text, containing both planned steps and adopted constraint rules.","limitations":"Does not account for the residual team-burnout and client-trust risks if the discovery phase turns out to be ineffective.","role":"current","role_interpretation":"The user's provisional action plan to conduct limited discovery phase without a delivery guarantee, while simultaneously scoping the reliability backlog.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-current-01-fc39b24e8a2855","semantic_status":"supported","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e057","stance_expression_kind":"provisional_intention_or_plan","stance_object_interpretation":"Offer Northline three focused sessions over two weeks to document workflow with an explicit baseline of no build commitment","stance_object_kind":"action_or_proposal"},{"source_evidence_id":"e058","stance_expression_kind":"provisional_intention_or_plan","stance_object_interpretation":"Enforce a boundary where Lina leads the workflow sessions but is restricted from starting production code","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"},{"source_evidence_id":"e059","stance_expression_kind":"provisional_intention_or_plan","stance_object_interpretation":"Simultaneously define the minimum acceptable reliability backlog and core release targets during this discovery period","stance_object_kind":"action_or_proposal"},{"source_evidence_id":"e060","stance_expression_kind":"provisional_intention_or_plan","stance_object_interpretation":"Make the final decision only when the discovery insights, reliability costs, and core requirements are all formally laid out together","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"}]},{"evidence_ids":["e049","e061"],"fidelity_note":"Groups the user's outstanding worries that remain unaddressed by the provisional framework.","limitations":"These risks depend largely on external variables such as Northline's organizational shifts and internal staff dynamics.","role":"qualification","role_interpretation":"Active counterpressures, client-management risks, and internal staff limitations that threaten to invalidate or reopen the provisional plan.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-qualification-01-40be86a9c0f1e3","semantic_status":"supported","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e049","stance_expression_kind":"counterpressure","stance_object_interpretation":"A delayed timeline could result in losing the key Northline operations contact who understands the problem best","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e061","stance_expression_kind":"counterpressure","stance_object_interpretation":"The 'no production code' restriction might waste Lina's primary learning mechanism and Northline might still interpret the boundary as a rejection","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"}]}],"schema_version":"lolla.simulated_reliability_joint_mechanism_input.v1","source_refs":[{"path":"research/designed-ambiguous-pool-v1-2026-07-10/development-cases/amb1-case01-product-scope.txt","sha256":"7ff5874289565a75ce3841350fe11f77528cf94544eb86b28d56491e39c92a73"}]}

Return exactly nine assessments, one for every mechanism_id and no duplicates. Use user role records to assign user_process_status. Use assistant_contributions to assign vanilla_answer_coverage. operationalized means the assistant turned the concern into an actionable test, boundary, alternative, or reopening condition; acknowledged_only means it merely mentioned the concern; not_covered means it did neither. Do not require the user to repeat an assistant repair before recognizing answer coverage, and do not mistake answer coverage for user adoption. route_uncovered_pressure is allowed only when user_process_status is unresolved and vanilla_answer_coverage is acknowledged_only or not_covered. An unresolved user process requires present or missing_protection whether or not it routes; routing_disposition alone controls routing. An ambiguous user process uses tension, while resolved and not_observed use not_applicable. not_observed also requires not_applicable coverage and both source arrays empty. Cite exact role_record_ids in source_role_record_ids and exact contribution_ids in source_assistant_contribution_ids. Do not output rationale, case prose, mental-model names, or invented IDs. The downstream routing projection remains fact-free and controlled-ID-only.
